    {
      "id": "oyBlXE6ClIi_8Xoz46fIW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5295.761904761905,
      "y": -1975.6667974562856,
      "width": 3931.6876179245282,
      "height": 3076.6666666666656,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 243552516,
      "version": 252,
      "versionNonce": 965157508,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788860490811,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Problem in Plain Terms\ncart_items is temporary state: if you delete a variant, it makes total sense to\nremove it from people's shopping bags using onDelete: \"cascade\".\n\norder_items is legal/accounting history: if you delete a variant, you cannot delete\nthe past sale row or let the query fail.\n\nImplement Soft Deletes for Products & Variants: Add an isActive boolean column\n(defaulting to true) to both products and product_variants tables instead of\nrunning hard SQL DELETE commands.\n\nVariant Deactivation Cleanup: When an admin marks a specific variant as isActive:\nfalse, immediately delete all occurrences of that variant_id from the cart_items\ntable using a transaction.\n\nProduct Deactivation Cascade: When an admin sets a parent product to isActive:\nfalse, set all associated child variants to isActive: false and delete all those child\nvariants from cart_items.\n\nStorefront Catalog Filtering: Ensure public catalog and browsing queries filter\nresults with where: and(eq(products.isActive, true), eq(product_variants.isActive,\ntrue)) so inactive items are hidden from shoppers.\n\nProtect Order History: Leave past sales records in order_items untouched during\nsoft deletes so historical invoices, analytics, and accounting records remain\ncompletely intact.",
      "fontSize": 94.66666666666663,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Problem in Plain Terms\ncart_items is temporary state: if you delete a variant, it makes total sense to remove it from people's shopping bags using onDelete: \"cascade\".\n\norder_items is legal/accounting history: if you delete a variant, you cannot delete the past sale row or let the query fail.\n\nImplement Soft Deletes for Products & Variants: Add an isActive boolean column (defaulting to true) to both products and product_variants tables instead of running hard SQL DELETE commands.\n\nVariant Deactivation Cleanup: When an admin marks a specific variant as isActive: false, immediately delete all occurrences of that variant_id from the cart_items table using a transaction.\n\nProduct Deactivation Cascade: When an admin sets a parent product to isActive: false, set all associated child variants to isActive: false and delete all those child variants from cart_items.\n\nStorefront Catalog Filtering: Ensure public catalog and browsing queries filter results with where: and(eq(products.isActive, true), eq(product_variants.isActive, true)) so inactive items are hidden from shoppers.\n\nProtect Order History: Leave past sales records in order_items untouched during soft deletes so historical invoices, analytics, and accounting records remain completely intact.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xm0qpS9NM677e6cA7h6wD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5315.761904761905,
      "y": 1634.3332025437144,
      "width": 3931.6876179245282,
      "height": 354.9999999999999,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1047866172,
      "version": 614,
      "versionNonce": 1959488004,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788863177477,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now if anybody delete there account then we just soft delete it because that\nuser_id is also connected to the addresses and addresses and userid is also\nconnected to the order or to say sales history so basiucally we just do this",
      "fontSize": 94.66666666666663,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now if anybody delete there account then we just soft delete it because that user_id is also connected to the addresses and addresses and userid is also connected to the order or to say sales history so basiucally we just do this",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b6Wvf9eG541h8ZxmXlS_u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5325.761904761905,
      "y": 2929.3332025437144,
      "width": 3931.6876179245282,
      "height": 236.66666666666657,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1586799804,
      "version": 762,
      "versionNonce": 123177348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788863177477,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So, that if the user wanna re-register it he can do that with the same number or\nemail.",
      "fontSize": 94.66666666666663,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So, that if the user wanna re-register it he can do that with the same number or email.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
